\\ constants.6502 - the screen's geometry and the well's, in the model's units (docs/model.md), and the
\\ palette's codes (D10).

\\ The screen: MODE 2, 64 characters by 28 rows (P1), at &33E8 so the well's first byte is on a page, an
\\ even one (D18): each row of the well is a page, and the 6502 draws by columns from the well's first

ScreenColumns = 64						; byte columns: 128 MODE 2 pixels
ScreenRows = 28
RowBytes = ScreenColumns * 8			; 512
ScreenBytes = RowBytes * ScreenRows		; &3800
ScreenAddr = GenScreenAddr
ScreenEnd = GenScreenEnd
WellAddr = GenWellAddr
ASSERT ScreenEnd == ScreenAddr + ScreenBytes AND WellAddr MOD 512 == 0
ScreenHSyncPos = 98 - (80 - ScreenColumns) DIV 2
ScreenVSyncPos = 35 - (32 - ScreenRows) DIV 2
VSyncPulseWidth = 2

\\ The layout (layout.py, D13): the checker's margin, then the left wall at column 2, the well's 32 byte
\\ columns inside, the right wall, and the panel's boxes in the checker beyond. A unit is a scanline, half a
\\ MODE 2 pixel (P2): x counts from the well's left edge (D18), y from the screen's top.

WallLeftCol = GenWallLeftCol
WellCol = GenWellCol
WellColumns = GenWellCols
WallRightCol = GenWallRightCol
FloorRow = GenFloorRow
FloorLine = GenFloorLine
RimLine = GenRimLine					; a ball poking above this, touching another, is failing

\\ The ball codes: the odd-parity logical colours (D10), and the physical colours (colours.py)

CodeR = 1:CodeG = 2:CodeB = 4:CodeY = 7:CodeM = 8:CodeC = 11:CodeW = 13:CodeP = 14

\\ The physical colours, in the ULA's numbering

Black = 0:Red = 1:Green = 2:Yellow = 3:Blue = 4:Magenta = 5:Cyan = 6:White = 7
